**C4. Tests and names.** *Branch 1:* in `wt-b772-a-head` and `wt-b772-a-base` (heavy, one at a time): `dotnet restore`, Release build of `api/tests/HpsmPoc.Api.Tests` (0 warnings, 0 errors expected: print rc and the warning count; the repo may treat warnings as errors), the class `PkcsInPackageTests` three times at the head (33/0/0 expected; seconds per run), the class at the base (25/0/0), then the WHOLE Api test project on SQLite once at the head and once at the base with a `.trx` logger (expect 2097 / 0 / 13 and 2089 / 0 / 13; the figures move with SDK and main, print yours and reconcile), **names**: lost and added full test names from the two `.trx` files (the time-seeded `assertion:` argument of `An_assertion_that_is_not_valid_is_401` masked; expect lost 0, added exactly the 8 new rows; control: one name dropped from a scratch copy reads lost 1). If load or time allows only one whole run, run the head and cut the base whole run (say so: names-lost is then UNMEASURED except for the class). Row seconds of the new rows (builder: 0.5 to 1.1 s each): a row over 20 s is a Minor. *Branch 2:* at main, at commit 1 and at the head: the reader file alone (34 expected at each), `test_security_baseline.py` alone (85 at main, 85 at commit 1, 89 at the head), and the WHOLE infra suite exactly as CI runs it, from `infra/`: `BICEP='<.tools/bicep/bicep>' python3 tests/test_security_baseline.py` (the `ci.yml` `infra` job runs `bash infra/scripts/validate.sh`, whose line 21 is `BICEP="$BICEP" python3 tests/test_security_baseline.py`; read it), at the head (266 expected) and at main (262); the epilogue figures `ResourceWarnings: 0` and `Files still open: 0` must print; also under `python3 -I`. Under `/usr/bin/python3` (3.9.6) the builder reports ONE pre-existing failure in `test_resource_hygiene.py` at main and at both commits: reproduce it at MAIN first (a failure you reproduce at main is a Note, not the branch's); the runner's Python is UNMEASURED. Names: reader 34 -> 34, security file 85 -> 89, whole infra 262 -> 266, lost 0 (control as above). Repeat the new guard tests 5 times each (20 x is the builder's; say 5): 0 red.

