## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker (per branch):* a path beyond the branch's paths; an `api/**` non-listed, `web/**`, `.github/**` or other `infra/**` byte; **a byte outside an XML comment in either csproj, or a changed pin line** (and that one is also a STOP for tier 1); a deleted, reordered or edited existing line of `PkcsInPackageTests.cs`; code (not docstring) changed in commit 1 of branch 2 (AST unequal); an existing assertion of `test_security_baseline.py` loosened, deleted or made conditional (the three removed lines are exactly the `loop =` line and the two `DISPATCH_LOOP` regex lines); a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id or a `B###` token (other than the carried-over one) in an added line or a message; a skip/sleep/retry/environment gate added to a test; the branch's head moved; a textual conflict; a secret; a CodeQL alert open on a head; a failing test at the head (class or suite, after the file is re-run alone twice, and the red NOT reproduced at main); a build with a warning that fails it.
*Major, class SAME:* **(M1) a new row that cannot fail:** a builder-named mutant that leaves green a row it is claimed to turn red; a row asserting only `Throws<Exception>`/`ThrowsAny`; a guard test of branch 2 that stays green under g1-g5; **(M2) a pin weakened:** any assertion of an existing row changed; **(M3)** the unmutated head class or suite not measured at all. *Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (33 class rows; 2097 / 0 / 13 within the SDK/main drift you explain; names lost 0; 266 infra tests; AST equal; csproj comment-only; 10 of 10 plants red and 25 of 25 harmless green; survivors 0 of the named set); a docstring sentence a plant contradicts (C1-B).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* the survivors u3 and g7 if they survive (row-strength gaps, with the killing fixture named); the DISCLOSED guard holes of branch 2 (`if (false)`, a delay after the pass, a `return` before the timer, `FeedbackModule` text read with comments); the two imprecise docstring sentences left; the pre-existing Python 3.9 failure (reproduced at main); `const PkcsListing` as a helper member (the builder asks; say it is harmless); the `B254` header carried on a reworded line; `HPSMPOC-355` in a code comment; unsigned commits; two commits instead of one on branch 1 (the second rewords comments and a temp-folder prefix, a squash lands them as one); no PR yet so no CI to read; SDK 10.0.402 here against CI's floating SDK (UNMEASURED-ON-SDK-10.0.403).
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes a new row unable to fail, or a claim in a docstring the code contradicts, is at least Major SAME or DIFFERENT; a thing that only narrows how strong a row is, stays true to the commission and is disclosed, is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Round 1 of 2 per class: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row and the number.**
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs the branch's checks clean and measured, every builder-named mutant red as claimed, survivors 0 (Notes aside), 0 findings above Note, and its CI predicates read (`UNMEASURED-ON-SQLSERVER` for branch 1 caps it at **GO WITH FINDINGS (conditional: the `api-other-and-feedback` shard and the `api` job not run; Tuesday reads them on the PR)** unless the PR's shard already exists and is read; branch 2's `infra` job likewise until its PR exists: its local whole-infra run is the substitute, not CI). GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major of that branch. NOT GATED = that head moved, or a moved guarded region. A security-shaped finding or a csproj byte outside a comment is a STOP for tier 1.
**VERDICT LINES (one place, binding).** **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B772: PENDING`; verdict form, ONE line, both branches):** `GATE VERDICT B772: b767 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 784dc97 (round 1 of 2 on class "api test rows for the three deps-entry checks of the Pkcs-in-package guard, plus csproj comment words" - delta <3 paths, numstat 113/0 2/2 1/1 y/n; csproj comment-only by program y/n with control fired y/n; existing lines kept y/n; hygiene y/n> - mutants <named set n of 8 red as claimed, before-table n of 3 green 25/25, u1-u4 n red as predicted, survivors <names|none>; c0 y/n; c-fail y/n> - tests <class 33/0/0 x3; whole Api SQLite n/n/n vs base n/n/n; names lost n added n> - CI <read; UNMEASURED-ON-SQLSERVER; PR y/n> - merge <rc n> - gitleaks rc <n>) | b768 <verdict> @ a3fa1c0 (round 1 of 2 on class "infra: the shard reader's docstring plus the dispatcher stays-awake guard rows" - delta <2 commits, 2 paths, 23/13 and 199/3 y/n; AST equal y/n with control fired y/n; docstring plants n of n as the sentences say; hygiene y/n> - mutants <g1-g7 n red as predicted, survivors <names|none>; builder plants 5 red + 5 green at head y/n, base reproduces the blind spot n of 5; c0 y/n; c-fail y/n> - tests <reader 34/34/34; security file 85/85/89; whole infra 262 -> 266 under python3 -I and the CI form; lost n added n> - CI <read; PR y/n> - merge <rc n; pair together rc n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks C1, C1-A, C1-B, C3, C4, C5, C6 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B772a-n` (branch 1), `B772b-n` (branch 2) and `B772s-n` (shared), each with severity, class SAME or DIFFERENT for a Major with the rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY ("none" is valid), the mutant tables (mutant, edit, predicted red set, actual red set BY NAME), the names tables, the CI table (check, predicate, status), FOR TUESDAY (each branch's verdict in plain words; whether its head-pinned squash can go, with the exact commands below; what is still required before each can (the PR must exist and its required contexts be satisfied under the product owner's rulings); the Q-question on B734's class if you raised it; the Notes as candidate decisions), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED** (at least: SQL Server and the shard; the `api` job in CI; SDK 10.0.403; the runner's Python; the real GitHub parse of the workflow; guard behaviour on a C# compiler; cells and mutants you cut). **Last line of STATUS: ONE line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B772 b767 b767/hpsmpoc-355-pkcs-rows @ 784dc97 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 1 of 2<; conditional: ...>) || b768 b768/hpsmpoc-356-228-infra-tests @ a3fa1c0 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 1 of 2<; conditional: ...>) on main <sha7>` (main by `git/matching-refs/heads/main` at verdict), with the findings ids, severities and classes in the line above it, or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

